    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d325">

                <pb facs="0605" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg573"/>

                <head>325. Telegram From the Embassy in Lebanon to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d325-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-09-19T11:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 19,
                                1958—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1627. Repeated London Exclusive for Admiral Holloway. Re Deptel 1273<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d325-f2"/> I believe we should retain initiative in announcing
                    withdrawal of all US forces from Lebanon by October 15 in order to forestall
                    adverse propaganda possibilities outlined Embtel 1560.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d325-f3"/> However, I believe we could usefully arrange with Chehab
                    and Prime Minister of new government for a joint US–Lebanon release outlining
                    details of this phased withdrawal.</p>
                <p>I do not consider it either feasible or desirable to work out some announcement
                    with Chamoun: (A) Because Chamoun himself is deeply opposed to early withdrawal
                    of US forces; and (B) an announcement involving ex-president would not sit well
                    with new president.</p>
                <pb facs="0606" n="574" xml:id="pg574"/>
                <p>Re final paragraph reference telegram, it is unnecessary to stress to Chehab that
                    withdrawal take place in logical, dignified and orderly fashion since this has
                    been general’s concept from the beginning. Throughout many conversations Admiral
                    Holloway and I have had with Chehab he has shown a soldier’s appreciation of
                    need for phased movement and full comprehension withdrawal must take place in an
                    orderly fashion with maximum of cooperation from Lebanese Government and armed
                    forces.</p>
                <p>Recommendation: That I be authorized to negotiate with Chehab tentative text of a
                    joint communiqué indicating, however, that initial release will come from US
                    side either from Washington or USDel UNGA.</p>
                <p>General Adams, Admirals Loud and Yeager concur.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">McClintock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
